trait-name-TraitParacusia = Paracusia
trait-description-TraitParacusia =
    You hear things that aren't there. Whispers, footsteps, voices calling your name —
    sometimes even snippets of conversations that never happened. Harmless to your body,
    but it grows worse the longer you stay conscious.

trait-name-TraitParacusiaAuditory = Auditory Paracusia
trait-description-TraitParacusiaAuditory =
    Silence rarely stays silent for you. Your mind fills the gaps with sounds that have no source,
    subtle at first, then harder to ignore as exhaustion sets in. What you hear may feel perfectly real,
    even when nothing around you made a sound.
